                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> 45% of fresher analyst postings ask for it, rising to 65% at mid level. About 4 in 5 Power BI or Tableau postings also ask for it.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>2. Make Excel and statistics your baseline.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> About 42% and 45% of fresher postings ask for them, at every level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>3. Add one BI tool.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> Power BI goes from 23% of fresher postings to 50% of senior ones, and Tableau from 20% to 40%. Either works, so pick one and build projects with it.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>4. Add Python after that.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> It’s in 34% of fresher analyst postings, against 80% of data scientist postings.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>5. Start with the biggest hiring cities.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> Bengaluru has 45% of jobs that name a city, then Delhi NCR (15%), Hyderabad (9%) and Pune (8.5%). Remote roles are a further market.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
